{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Whom he has not designated, etc.</b> The reason <b>lo</b> is written with alef yet read with vav may be explained according to the statement of the Sages, of blessed memory (Kiddushin 19a), that designation (ye'ud) is only with her consent, and they derived this in Kiddushin from the word ״יְעָדָהּ״ — that her consent is required. Therefore, corresponding to the impediment coming from his side, He said <b>אִם רָעָה בְּעֵינֵי אֲדֹנֶיהָ</b>, and corresponding to the impediment coming from her side — if she does not consent to the matter — He said <b>אֲשֶׁר לֹא יְעָדָהּ</b>, for the matter was not with her knowledge; either one of these constitutes an impediment. And His saying <b>וְהֶפְדָּהּ</b> means — only then is she eligible for redemption, and [her master] deducts from her redemption value; but other than this, if he designated her, there is no possibility of her going out as stated." "<b>To a foreign people.</b> Meaning: even though I told you that a man may sell his daughter, he may not sell her to a foreign people. Furthermore, even if he already did the deed and betrayed her and sold her — his sale is no sale, as it says <b>לֹא יִמְשֹׁל</b> etc. <b>בְּבִגְדוֹ</b> etc., and the right of both buyer and seller is voided." "It further intends, according to their statement (Kiddushin 19a), that a father may sell his daughter to those disqualified for her — a widow to a High Priest, and so forth — and this is His saying <b>לְעַם נָכְרִי</b>, meaning: to a foreign people he may not give her authority; but a man who is foreign to her yet belongs to a people that is not foreign — is permitted."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:31:35.432038954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}